Development plans

* Dynamic config will be used for matching raw error messages with code.
** Dynamic config will be release with a separate release, then it is easier to fill
* Numbers will be replace with # in error messages in conf keys
** e.g. {{Senha inválida. Tem mais 4 tentativas.}} will be replaced with {{Senha inválida. Tem mais # tentativas.}}
* Code will handle 2 types of structures of errors, examples:
** {{[{"code":"tax_authority_credentials_not_valid","message":"Senha inválida. Tem mais 4 tentativas.\\nVerifique se não está a utilizar maiúsculas ou minúsculas indevidamente.","type":"tax_authority"}]}}
** {{{"text":"API Error","apiStatus":400,"registerResult":{"errors":[{"code":"field_not_valid","field":"address.postal_code","message":"address.postal_code must follow the format 0000-000","type":"validation"}],"status":"failed"}}}}
* Tests for both cases are being written

If we issue PoA we need to follow Bolt PoA drafting process. In the initial PoA some essential parts was missing, like:

* Subdelegation is not allowed;
* In the case of multilingual PoAs, the English version should prevail in case of discrepancies;

Please ask them to comment and suggest needed changes in the word document so we have one common version we work on. Signing will only be initiated when we will agree on the final wording of PoA.

