{noformat}1. Prepare required resources (new S3 + tune IAM stuff);
2. Stop the archive and wait for connectors to put all the data to S3;
3. Move db_archive.taxify_pricing_order.* folders to the new bucket. Most probably we'll also have to rename them to db_archive.searchable.*. Not yet sure how long this might take, but shouldn't be too long;
4. Pause existing `archiver` kafka connector;
5. Change connectors config:
        Existing archiver connector will handle everything, beside `db_archive.searchable.*` with the next regex: `db_archive.(?!searchable).*`
        New connector will handle `db_archive.searchable.*` with the next regex: db_archive.taxify_pricing_order.*
6. Remove `taxify_pricing_order` topics from kafka. This way we won't need to wait for 4 days to remove the data. And topics will be created automatically upon first produce request.
7. Resume both `archiver` and the new connectors;
8. Redeploy archive-searcher to point to the new bucket;
9. Resume archive and ensure new data arriving in the new bucket;
10. Delete the data in the old bucket;
11. Change `archive-restorer` and `archive-alter` to be able to access both buckets.{noformat}

